daemon/dev8030/drv8030: include hotplug_rpc.h

drv_dev.c calls dev8030_hotplug_event() (declared in the sibling
daemon/dev8030/hotplug_rpc.h, already on this target's include path via
CMakeLists.txt's "target_include_directories(drv8030 PRIVATE ../)") but
never includes that header -- every other bus backend that calls the same
function (usb8030/usb_dev.c, sdio8030/sdio_dev.c, uart8030/uart_dev.c)
does. Harmless under older/laxer compilers (implicit-declaration was only
a warning), but fails outright as an error on GCC 14
(-Wimplicit-function-declaration is an error by default for C99+ there):

    drv_dev.c:345:17: error: implicit declaration of function
    'dev8030_hotplug_event' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

USING_8030DRV (the /dev/ar_mdev0 backend this board's daemon build uses,
alongside USING_8030USB) is the only bus backend that hits this, which is
presumably why it went unnoticed upstream.

diff --git a/daemon/dev8030/drv8030/drv_dev.c b/daemon/dev8030/drv8030/drv_dev.c
index 568e508..82ba34c 100644
--- a/daemon/dev8030/drv8030/drv_dev.c
+++ b/daemon/dev8030/drv8030/drv_dev.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include "com_log.h"
 #include "dev8030.h"
+#include "hotplug_rpc.h"
 #include "list.h"
 #include "rpc_node.h"
 #include "timspec_helper.h"
